  "question": {
    "text": "<strong> Paragraph: </strong>\r\n\r\nLet $\\psi_{1}:[0, \\infty) \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}, \\psi_{2}:[0, \\infty) \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}, f:[0, \\infty) \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ and $g:[0, \\infty) \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ be functions such that $f(0)=g(0)=0$,\r\n\r\n$\\psi_{1}(x)=e^{-x}+x, \\quad x \\geq 0$,\r\n\r\n$\\psi_{2}(x)=x^{2}-2 x-2 e^{-x}+2, \\quad x \\geq 0$,\r\n\r\n$f(x)=\\int_{-x}^{x}\\left(|t|-t^{2}\\right) e^{-t^{2}} d t, \\quad x>0$\r\n\r\nand $g(x)=\\int_{0}^{x^{2}} \\sqrt{t} e^{-t} d t, \\quad x>0$\r\n\r\n<br> <strong> Question: </strong>\r\n\r\nWhich of the following statements is TRUE ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "OlLt3",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><msqrt><mi>ln</mi><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><msqrt><mi>ln</mi><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MqYPX",
      "text": "For every&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, there exists an&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#968;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>x</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MCorL",
      "text": "For every&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, there exists a&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#968;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#968;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>&#946;</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "GoYk6",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>&nbsp;is an increasing function on the interval&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
